199 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 89 0 R/E(No matter at what level managerial change is a definite, and the NCEFL is no exception - nearly 3 months since the beginning of the season and 8 clubs, and that\220s what I know have changed managers - from the Premier Division the latest is Retford United, although this one is slightly different as Ryan Hindle who has been their manager for the last four-and-a-half years and guided the team to promotion last season has left to take over at Step 3 side Ilkeston Town where he will have quite a task on as at present they are second bottom of the NPL Premier Division - other changes in the NCEFL Premier Division have seen Lee Morris leave Worsbrough Bridge to take over at Frickley Athletic, subsequently Worsbrough Bridge have appointed Conor Glavin 5 years at the club and with over 200 appearances as their new manager - Conor will act as a player/manager.)/Pg 19 0 R/K[2]>>
endobj

200 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 89 0 R/E(Keighley Town are the other Premier Division side to have recently appointed a new manager with James Gill taking over from Des Hazel.)/Pg 19 0 R/K[3]>>
endobj

201 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 89 0 R/E(The first Division has also seen some changes - South Leeds are now on their third manager this season, Nathan Cartman who took over in the close season left the club at the end of August and was replaced by Steve Stennett who has also now been replaced by Reece Mudd who founded the club in 2017 and managed them from then until 2025. )/Pg 19 0 R/K[4]>>
endobj

